From: Ziy engine fork <ziy@ziy.app>
Date: 2026-10-15
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] configure: declare --enable-ziy-fingerprinting, include it,
 and fail loudly if the gate and the shell disagree

Patch 1/2 gates a C++ delta on MOZ_ZIY_FINGERPRINTING. This patch declares the
option that defines it, makes the file reachable from the configure graph, and
adds a sanity check so a mismatch between the gate and the shipped prefs can
never build silently.

Three parts:

1. toolkit/ziy-fingerprinting.configure (new file) declares
   --enable-ziy-fingerprinting and set_define()s MOZ_ZIY_FINGERPRINTING from
   it. The value reaches every C++ TU through mozilla-config.h, the
   -include'd header built/moz.configure/toolchain.configure: defines_cpp_flags
   adds to OS_COMPILE_CFLAGS/OS_COMPILE_CXXFLAGS.

2. toolkit/moz.configure gains one include() line. This is the fix for the
   dead gate: configure.py:171 loads exactly ONE entry point, the root
   moz.configure, and every other .configure file must be pulled in by an
   include() -- there is no directory scan. Root moz.configure:519 does
   include(include_project_configure), init.configure:990 resolves that to
   browser/moz.configure, browser/moz.configure:54 includes
   ../toolkit/moz.configure, and toolkit/moz.configure included exactly five
   files (../js/moz.configure:480, ../build/moz.configure/node.configure:485,
   keyfiles.configure:1162, nss.configure:3175,
   update-programs.configure:4053) -- not this one. So the file landed on disk
   and was never executed: ac_add_options --enable-ziy-fingerprinting aborted
   at python/mozbuild/mozbuild/configure/__init__.py:564 ("Unknown option:
   %s"), and had that been suppressed the set_define would never have run and
   patch 1's #ifdef would have been false, i.e. a GREEN BUILD OF STOCK GECKO.
   The line is appended at the end of the file, in the same comment-banner
   style as the five includes it joins, so the reverse apply is an exact
   restoration.

3. The gate check. Ziy's shell ships
   privacy.fingerprintingProtection.overrides="+AllTargets,-CSSPrefersColorScheme"
   (shell/mozilla.cfg:42, shell/browser/defaults/preferences/ziy.js:145). A
   build without the define would silently ship stock Gecko that ignores that
   carve-out -- the exact bug patch 1 fixes. configure is the only place that
   sees both the shell's prefs and the option value, so the check belongs
   there, and it fails at configure time rather than after hours of compile.
   Mechanism: configure_error() from build/moz.configure/util.configure:14
   ("Primarily for use in moz.configure templates to sanity check their inputs
   from moz.configure usage"), the same helper the engine uses for exactly this
   shape of check at toolkit/moz.configure:4497-4498. No C++ #error guard is
   added: a compile-time guard could only ever fire in a configuration where
   the code is already dead, whereas this one catches the disagreement itself.

The option defaults off, so a build with --disable-ziy-fingerprinting (or with
the override removed from the shell) is stock Gecko, unchanged.


diff --git a/toolkit/moz.configure b/toolkit/moz.configure
index 2a0b994..d57b7d5 100644
--- a/toolkit/moz.configure
+++ b/toolkit/moz.configure
@@ -4640,3 +4640,8 @@ def libmegazord_artifacts(value):
 
 
 set_config("MOZ_LIBMEGAZORD_ARTIFACTS", libmegazord_artifacts)
+
+
+# Ziy engine fork: the configure gate for the C++ patch set
+# ==============================================================
+include("ziy-fingerprinting.configure")
diff --git a/toolkit/ziy-fingerprinting.configure b/toolkit/ziy-fingerprinting.configure
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1f5f378
--- /dev/null
+++ b/toolkit/ziy-fingerprinting.configure
@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+# Ziy engine fork: the C++ patch gate.
+#
+# Declares the ONE configure option the C++ patch set is gated on:
+# --enable-ziy-fingerprinting. Its value lands in mozilla-config.h as the
+# MOZ_ZIY_FINGERPRINTING define, which is what the #ifdefs in
+# patches/0001-*.patch test.
+#
+# WHY AN OPTION AND NOT A BARE -D: ./mach configure hard-fails on any option it
+# does not know ("Unknown option: %s", python/mozbuild/mozbuild/configure/
+# __init__.py:564). An undeclared -DMOZ_ZIY_FINGERPRINTING in .mozconfig would
+# abort configure before the build starts. Declaring the option here is what
+# makes .mozconfig's `ac_add_options --enable-ziy-fingerprinting` legal, and
+# what makes `--disable-ziy-fingerprinting` produce a stock-Gecko build.
+#
+# WHY THIS SHIPS AS A PATCH: the file lands on the pristine source tree at
+# patch-apply time, and it is the only reason the gate is switchable without
+# hand-editing a generated header.
+#
+# HOW IT IS REACHED: this file is NOT discovered by a directory scan — Gecko's
+# configure loads exactly one entry point (configure.py:171 -> root
+# moz.configure) and every other .configure file must be pulled in by an
+# `include()`. toolkit/moz.configure includes exactly five files and none of
+# them was this one, which is why the gate was dead before the second hunk of
+# this patch added the include line there.
+
+# Declared as a real option so ac_add_options can pass it.
+option(
+    "--enable-ziy-fingerprinting",
+    help="Compile Ziy's C++ fingerprinting delta into the engine "
+         "(disabling this yields a stock-Gecko build)",
+)
+
+# The value flows into mozilla-config.h — the -include'd header every C++ TU
+# receives (build/moz.configure/toolchain.configure: defines_cpp_flags) — as
+# MOZ_ZIY_FINGERPRINTING, the macro the patch's #ifdefs test.
+@depends("--enable-ziy-fingerprinting")
+def ziy_fingerprinting(value):
+    if value:
+        return True
+
+
+set_define("MOZ_ZIY_FINGERPRINTING", ziy_fingerprinting)
+
+
+# WHY A GUARD AND NOTHING MORE: the failure this patch set MUST NOT be able to
+# have silently. Ziy's shell ships
+# privacy.fingerprintingProtection.overrides="+AllTargets,-CSSPrefersColorScheme"
+# (shell/mozilla.cfg:42 lockPref, shell/browser/defaults/preferences/ziy.js:145
+# pref). If a build were produced WITHOUT the define, the engine would ignore
+# the shipped -CSSPrefersColorScheme carve-out — exactly the bug
+# patches/0001-*.patch exists to fix — and the build would still look green.
+# Checking it here is the only place that can fail loudly before hours of
+# compile, because it is the only place that sees both the shell's prefs and
+# the configure value. The precedent is the engine's own configure_error
+# (build/moz.configure/util.configure:14, "Primarily for use in moz.configure
+# templates to sanity check their inputs from moz.configure usage"), used at
+# toolkit/moz.configure:4497-4498 for exactly this shape of sanity check, and
+# built on the same @depends(...)+function pattern as the `set_define` above
+# (update-programs.configure:50-51 is the same shape: @depends over an option,
+# then a plain function).
+@depends(
+    "--enable-ziy-fingerprinting",
+    build_environment,
+)
+@checking("that the Ziy gate is consistent with the shipped prefs")
+@imports(_from="__builtin__", _import="open")
+@imports("os")
+def ziy_fingerprinting_gate_check(ziy_fingerprinting, build_environment):
+    topsrcdir = os.path.realpath(
+        os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), "..", "..")
+    )
+    for rel in (
+        "shell/mozilla.cfg",
+        "shell/browser/defaults/preferences/ziy.js",
+    ):
+        path = os.path.join(topsrcdir, rel)
+        if not os.path.exists(path):
+            continue
+        with open(path, "r") as f:
+            for line in f:
+                if "-CSSPrefersColorScheme" in line:
+                    break
+            else:
+                continue
+            if ziy_fingerprinting is not True:
+                configure_error(
+                    f"{rel} ships the -CSSPrefersColorScheme override, which "
+                    "needs patches/0001-*.patch compiled in, but "
+                    "--enable-ziy-fingerprinting is not set: the build would "
+                    "silently ship stock Gecko that ignores the carve-out. "
+                    "Pass `ac_add_options --enable-ziy-fingerprinting`, or "
+                    "drop the override from the shell."
+                )
+            break
